<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch13-chapter-ci-differences" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Estimating the Difference between Two Parameters</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> This chapter will teach students to construct confidence intervals for a difference in population means and a difference in population 
      proportions using bootstrapping. Students learn how to interpret these confidence intervals and make statements about effect size and 
      practical importance.</p>
  </introduction>


  <objectives>
    <ol>
    <li>Explore...</li>

    <li>Learn...</li>

    <li>Understand...</li>

    <li>Apply...</li>
  </ol>
  </objectives>


  

